# @skill devos-code-architect
# DevOS Code Organization & Architecture Skill
# Specializes in modular, well-structured code with 30-line file limit

description: |
  Expert in DevOS architecture: modular code organization, React Native + FastAPI 
  development, LangGraph agents, and maintaining code standards.

expertise:
  - React Native (Expo) patterns
  - FastAPI + LangGraph agent design
  - Modular architecture (max 30 lines per file)
  - TypeScript & Python best practices
  - Mobile-first UI/UX

rules:
  - Every file: maximum 30 lines (enforced)
  - Every function/block: exactly one comment explaining purpose
  - Type hints on all functions (Python) or explicit return types (TypeScript)
  - No hardcoded values (use constants)
  - No console.log/print in production
  - All I/O operations: async/non-blocking
  - Split concerns: separate files for UI, logic, API, DB

fileOrganization:
  frontend:
    - app/ → Routes (file-based routing)
    - components/ → UI (max 30 lines each)
    - hooks/ → Custom hooks (max 30 lines)
    - services/ → API & storage
    - utils/ → Helpers
    - types/ → TypeScript interfaces
    - config/ → Constants & env
  
  backend:
    - agents/nodes/ → LangGraph nodes (30 lines each)
    - agents/tools/ → Agent tools (30 lines each)
    - api/ → REST endpoints (30 lines each)
    - db/ → Database models
    - mocks.py → Test data

commentStyle: |
  // Single comment explaining PURPOSE (not WHAT)
  function fetchUser(id: string): Promise<User> { ... }

refactoringPatterns: |
  - File too large? → Split into smaller files
  - Function > 30 lines? → Extract helper functions
  - Multiple concerns? → Create separate modules
  - Hardcoded values? → Move to constants.ts/.py

documentation:
  - README.md → Project overview
  - QUICK_START.md → Setup guide
  - PROJECT_STRUCTURE.md → Folder layout
  - docs/ → Detailed guides
  - .instructions.md → Code standards
  - .agent.md → Agent specialization

invokedFor: |
  - Creating new modules/components
  - Refactoring large files
  - Architecture decisions
  - Code reviews
  - Setting up new features
  - Best practices consultation

---

When helping with DevOS:
1. Enforce 30-line file limit
2. Add one comment per function explaining purpose
3. Use type hints everywhere
4. Split into multiple files if needed
5. Reference docs/ folder for detailed guides
